AMDGPU: FLAT accesses on GFX6-GFX8 initialise and use M0

Generic (gfx6-gfx8; gfx803 is where it was found and tested).

Verified on an RX 590 (gfx803) with clang built from ROCm llvm-project
rocm-6.4.4 (d366fa84) with this patch on top of
0001-amdgpu-callee-implicit-kernarg.patch.

WHY
---
On gfx6-gfx8 a FLAT load, store or atomic whose address falls in the LDS
aperture is range-checked against M0, like a DS instruction (AMDGPUUsage:
"Flat access to LDS requires hardware aperture setup and M0 (GFX7-GFX8)
register setup"). LLVM initialises M0 (s_mov_b32 m0, -1) only for accesses
whose address space is LOCAL or REGION, and the FLAT instructions do not
read M0, so an access through a generic pointer that points into LDS runs
with whatever M0 holds. With M0 below the address the access is dropped:
stores are lost and loads return 0, with no fault.

It shows when the pointer is not resolved to an LDS address at compile
time, for example a non-inlined function returning a pointer into a
__shared__ array:

  __attribute__((noinline)) __device__ int *lds_slot(int i) {
      __shared__ int a[64]; return a + i; }
  ... *lds_slot(t) = v; __syncthreads(); x = *lds_slot(63 - t);

On gfx803 every value read back is 0; with `s_mov_b32 m0, -1` at kernel
entry, or with the function inlined (DS instructions), it is correct.

WHAT
----
- glueCopyToM0LDSInit glues M0 = -1 to FLAT-address-space loads, stores and
  atomics on targets where ldsRequiresM0Init() holds, as it does for LOCAL.
- SIFixSGPRCopies adds an implicit use of M0 to those FLAT instructions
  before it merges M0 initialisations. Without the use the glued init is a
  dead definition, and the merge and later passes move it past the access
  or drop it (the first store after a call above stayed unguarded).
Global and constant accesses, which gfx8 also emits as flat_*, carry
address space 1 or 4 in their memory operand and are not touched. GlobalISel
is not changed; HIP selects with SelectionDAG.

Measured with the patched clang (RX 590): the probe above passes 64 of 64
values (every value reads 0 without this patch), with `s_mov_b32 m0, -1`
emitted before the generic store.

diff --git a/llvm/lib/Target/AMDGPU/AMDGPUISelDAGToDAG.cpp b/llvm/lib/Target/AMDGPU/AMDGPUISelDAGToDAG.cpp
index b84682cd5..da7155ea1 100644
--- a/llvm/lib/Target/AMDGPU/AMDGPUISelDAGToDAG.cpp
+++ b/llvm/lib/Target/AMDGPU/AMDGPUISelDAGToDAG.cpp
@@ -413,6 +413,11 @@ SDNode *AMDGPUDAGToDAGISel::glueCopyToM0LDSInit(SDNode *N) const {
   if (AS == AMDGPUAS::LOCAL_ADDRESS) {
     if (Subtarget->ldsRequiresM0Init())
       return glueCopyToM0(N, CurDAG->getTargetConstant(-1, SDLoc(N), MVT::i32));
+  } else if (AS == AMDGPUAS::FLAT_ADDRESS) {
+    // A generic pointer can hit the LDS aperture, and gfx6-8 range-check that
+    // access against M0 as well; an uninitialised M0 drops the access.
+    if (Subtarget->ldsRequiresM0Init())
+      return glueCopyToM0(N, CurDAG->getTargetConstant(-1, SDLoc(N), MVT::i32));
   } else if (AS == AMDGPUAS::REGION_ADDRESS) {
     MachineFunction &MF = CurDAG->getMachineFunction();
     unsigned Value = MF.getInfo<SIMachineFunctionInfo>()->getGDSSize();
diff --git a/llvm/lib/Target/AMDGPU/SIFixSGPRCopies.cpp b/llvm/lib/Target/AMDGPU/SIFixSGPRCopies.cpp
index 65d76baac..d3677e5d2 100644
--- a/llvm/lib/Target/AMDGPU/SIFixSGPRCopies.cpp
+++ b/llvm/lib/Target/AMDGPU/SIFixSGPRCopies.cpp
@@ -774,6 +774,24 @@ bool SIFixSGPRCopies::runOnMachineFunction(MachineFunction &MF) {
   for (auto MI : PHINodes) {
     processPHINode(*MI);
   }
+  // On targets that range-check LDS accesses against M0, a FLAT access can
+  // reach LDS through the aperture, and selection glued an M0 init to it. The
+  // instruction itself does not read M0, which leaves that init dead: the
+  // merge below and later passes may then move it past the access or drop it.
+  if (ST.ldsRequiresM0Init()) {
+    for (MachineBasicBlock &MBB : MF) {
+      for (MachineInstr &MI : MBB) {
+        if (!TII->isFLAT(MI) || TII->isFLATGlobal(MI) || TII->isFLATScratch(MI) ||
+            MI.memoperands_empty() || MI.readsRegister(AMDGPU::M0, TRI))
+          continue;
+        if (llvm::any_of(MI.memoperands(), [](const MachineMemOperand *MMO) {
+              return MMO->getAddrSpace() == AMDGPUAS::FLAT_ADDRESS;
+            }))
+          MI.addOperand(MachineOperand::CreateReg(AMDGPU::M0, /*isDef=*/false,
+                                                  /*isImp=*/true));
+      }
+    }
+  }
   if (MF.getTarget().getOptLevel() > CodeGenOptLevel::None && EnableM0Merge)
     hoistAndMergeSGPRInits(AMDGPU::M0, *MRI, TRI, *MDT, TII);
 
